frequently asked questions about NetHack from rec.games.hack    (weekly post)

"what is NetHack?"
	a single-user, fantasy role-playing, computer game, a direct
	descendant of Hack (and Rogue before it).  the interface
	remains similar, but NetHack has a much richer feature set.

"what is the CURRENT VERSION?"
	NetHack 3.0j    {or 3.0 patchlevel 10, 3.0.10}

"where do i get the LATEST SOURCE or BINARIES?"
	ftp: linc.cis.upenn.edu  pub/NH3.0/*                   {130.91.6.8}
	uucp: uunet.uu.net    comp.sources.games archives      {FTP also}
	VMS: DECnet SPAN from ACDURS::SYS$LCL:[SRC.NETHACK]    {or 9583::}

"when will the NEXT VERSION be released and what will be different?"
	The development team will announce 3.1 when its ready ...

"who do i contact for BUG REPORTS or installation HELP?"
	nethack-bugs@linc.cis.upenn.edu     {development team address}
	don't ask for strategy tips, etc., that belongs in rec.games.hack.

"where do i go for MORE INFO a/o SPOILERS?"
	during play: "?" and "/" commands, fortune cookies and the Oracle.
	the (non-spoiler) guidebook which accompanies the game.
	explore-mode: nethack -X    {you start with a wand of wishing}
	spoilers: comp.sources.games/volume12/nh-spoilers2/*    {v5.35}

the references mentioned above should cover nearly all questions.

"what is WIZARD-MODE and how do i use it?"
	the game maintainer can use wizard-mode as a debugging aid.
	try: "nethack -u wizard -D"    or: "nethack -uWizard -D"    ...

"the DUNGEON COLLAPSED, can i RECOVER this game? and who is 'izchak'?"
	find the panic save file (*.e),	if it exists, and remove the
	".e" suffix.  note: "crashed" games usually cannot be recovered.

"i've undergone a POLYMORPH NAME CHANGE, how do i RESTORE my game?"
	in most implementations you have to tell the game your new
        name, as in: nethack -u "new name goes here"

"i've cleaned out the castle, where are the downstairs?"
	part of the challenge of nethack is figuring out mysteries like
	this.  relax!  the developers haven't left you trapped ...


